# SDD Framework

## Startup (every session)
Read these files in order before doing anything else:
1. `.specify/manifest.yml` — project name, scope, feature, workflow mode
2. `.specify/memory/constitution.md` — universal rules (Part 1) + project tech stack (Part 2)
3. `.specify/memory/summary-rules.md` — reading mode (auto/summary/full)
4. `.specify/memory/roles.yml` — RACI (who approves what)
5. `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` — language/file-type coding standards; apply each file's `applyTo` glob to any file you create or edit that matches it

Confirm: project.name, scope, feature, constitution status (GATE-1 passed?).
If constitution Part 2 is a DRAFT (not finalized) → remind the user to complete GATE-1 before /validate.

## Running Commands
To run any SDD command, read and follow the matching prompt file **exactly as written**:

| Command | Prompt File |
|---|---|
| create-context | `.github/prompts/create-context.prompt.md` |
| specify | `.github/prompts/specify.prompt.md` |
| checklist *(optional)* | `.github/prompts/checklist.prompt.md` |
| validate | `.github/prompts/validate.prompt.md` |
| analyze | `.github/prompts/analyze.prompt.md` |
| clarify | `.github/prompts/clarify.prompt.md` |
| plan-arch | `.github/prompts/plan-arch.prompt.md` |
| plan-hld | `.github/prompts/plan-hld.prompt.md` |
| plan-lld *(mvp+ only)* | `.github/prompts/plan-lld.prompt.md` |
| plan-adr *(mvp+ only)* | `.github/prompts/plan-adr.prompt.md` |
| task | `.github/prompts/task.prompt.md` |
| implement | `.github/prompts/implement.prompt.md` |
| release | `.github/prompts/release.prompt.md` |

**How to invoke in Cursor:** In the chat panel, type:
`Read and follow .github/prompts/specify.prompt.md exactly`

## Command Order
SPECIFY → [GATE-1] → /checklist (optional) → VALIDATE → ANALYZE → CLARIFY
→ PLAN-ARCH → PLAN-HLD → PLAN-LLD (mvp+) → PLAN-ADR (mvp+) → TASK → IMPLEMENT → RELEASE

Each step requires the previous one reviewed and approved before proceeding.

## Reading Mode (AI-2)
Default: `auto` — use `.summary.md` when present; if missing, read the full `.md` and generate the summary. See `.specify/memory/summary-rules.md` for the full decision tree.

## Core Rules (always enforced)
- No code before context.md is updated and spec + TASK are approved
- Constitution Part 2 must be finalized (GATE-1) before /validate
- Every class/component has a paired test in the same PR
- No hardcoded values — env vars only
- PRs stay within the line/file limits in manifest.yml
